1
00:00:00,630 --> 00:00:03,680
[UNCLE] The nomads attacked,
defeating our militia.

2
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:06,970
Without our forces,
it will be impossible

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:09,350
to prevent them
from entering the city.

4
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:12,350
When they arrive,
there'll be pillaging.

5
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:15,770
So, we'll need to hide our food
and valuables before then.

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,820
[Zumurrud grunts] We won't get
too much down here.

7
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,030
[ANIS] Mm...

8
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:25,740
[smirks]

9
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:27,580
[BOTH] Uh?

10
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,990
[both exclaim]

11
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:32,500
I'll lead my sons
to the mountains,

12
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,370
and we shall take shelter there.

13
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:36,290
Yes, good idea.

14
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:37,380
For right now,

15
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:40,050
you and Sitara
need to hide down in the cellar.

16
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:42,630
We will come back in three days.

17
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:45,680
Sitara, I leave Ms. Fatima
in your hands.

18
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,640
Sure! I'll keep her safe!

19
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,470
And we'll be seeing you soon.

20
00:00:49,510 --> 00:00:51,890
-Till then...
-You two take care!

21
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:55,690
[ANIS] Times like these bring me
back to my childhood.

22
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:58,270
We fled our city more times
than I can count.

23
00:00:58,310 --> 00:00:59,610
[ZUMURRUD]
You should at least feel

24
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:01,440
a little worried about all this!

25
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:02,940
[ANIS] I suppose so.

26
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:11,450
[SITARA] Mistress,
why don't you have some dates?

27
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:14,450
[FATIMA]
That sounds nice. Thank you.

28
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:17,790
In this cellar,

29
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:20,880
it feels as though the world
has come to a complete stop.

30
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:24,010
I can see the outside light
through here.

31
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:26,340
It has already come and gone
three times now.

32
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:28,720
So, that should mean Uncle
and the others

33
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,680
will be coming to get us soon.
But still...

34
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,350
If it takes them
a little longer,

35
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:35,440
thanks to all their
preparations,

36
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,850
we'll have plenty of supplies
to last us!

37
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,860
And your books
are safe here, too!

38
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,110
You're right.

39
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:42,780
Thank you, Sitara.

40
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,150
Having you with me
keeps my spirits high.

41
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:47,240
I haven't done anything!

42
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:48,950
Uh...

43
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,120
Come to think of it.

44
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,870
I wonder
if the nomads have read

45
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:54,910
about Euclid's
different theorems.

46
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,580
I'm not sure.

47
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:59,580
That said, I mustn't lose
a single volume.

48
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:01,750
My husband spent
his life collecting them.

49
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,050
[Sitara exclaims]

50
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:04,710
Yes, you're right.

51
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,510
[Fatima chuckles]
Sitara, I'm curious.

52
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:10,300
You care for Muhammad,
don't you?

53
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,260
[Sitara gasps, stutters]

54
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:16,430
Yes. I think highly of him.

55
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,940
There can't be many people
in the world

56
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:20,310
who are as intelligent.

57
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:21,560
[Fatima chuckles softly]

58
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:23,650
The boy takes after his father.

59
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:27,860
Bridling at the restrictions
of conservative theology.

60
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:30,700
But still...

61
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:33,080
The more he walks
his own path in life,

62
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,330
the more objections
and resistance he will face.

63
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,910
In such times,

64
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,040
there will be only one person
able to comfort him.

65
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:44,590
Sitara, that would be you.

66
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,010
[Sitara gasps]

67
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:48,300
I want you to serve my son.

68
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,590
As a human unto yourself.

69
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:54,560
♪

70
00:03:07,110 --> 00:03:08,320
[Sitara breathes softly]

71
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,070
[Fatima chuckles]

72
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:12,320
[Sitara breathes shakily]

73
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:14,200
I will.

74
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,410
-[footsteps]
-[thumping]

75
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,630
[SITARA AND FATIMA] Uh?

76
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:24,460
[FATIMA] It's my brother
and the girls.

77
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,090
We can finally come out.

78
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:27,550
[SITARA] Yes!

79
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,840
[BOTH] Hm.

80
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,600
[both grunt]

81
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:41,140
[Sitara gasps]

82
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,690
[Fatima exhales]

83
00:03:46,730 --> 00:03:47,820
[SITARA] Uh?

84
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:50,400
[Sitara breathes uneasily]

85
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,280
[footsteps approaching]

86
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:02,040
[Sitara breathes uneasily]

87
00:04:04,830 --> 00:04:06,630
[TOLUI] Ah...

88
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,010
[♪ opening theme song playing]

89
00:05:38,010 --> 00:05:40,260
[Sitara grunts]

90
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,600
[gasps]

91
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:51,770
I thank you, Sitara.

92
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:53,070
[SITARA] Of course.

93
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,240
-Stand back.
-[Sitara gasps]

94
00:05:57,530 --> 00:05:58,490
[Sitara grunts]

95
00:05:58,530 --> 00:05:59,620
Sitara.

96
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,160
Don't offer resistance.

97
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:04,450
Yes...

98
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:06,370
Mistress.

99
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:11,630
[SHIRA] Uh?

100
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,130
[Shira chuckles]

101
00:06:18,470 --> 00:06:20,010
[thudding]

102
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,940
[Sitara and Fatima
breathe uneasily]

103
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:43,990
[Fatima breathes shakily]

104
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,830
[Fatima, in English]
No! Not that book!

105
00:06:57,050 --> 00:06:58,300
[laughs]

106
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:15,230
[Fatima breathes shakily]

107
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:20,780
[grunts]

108
00:07:20,990 --> 00:07:23,320
[in English] "Whether they are
a man or woman,

109
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:24,700
cut off the hands of thieves

110
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:27,290
as punishment for the awful deed
they have done!"

111
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,210
-Sitara!
-It's not right.

112
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,670
That book doesn't belong to you,
so you must give it back!

113
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:58,190
[in English] My Master says
you are not to call him a thief.

114
00:07:58,230 --> 00:07:59,190
"Everything on this..."

115
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,190
[SITARA] This boy understands
our language.

116
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,200
"...The Genghis Khan."

117
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,330
[both gasp]

118
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:20,380
[Sitara trembles]

119
00:08:20,550 --> 00:08:21,800
-[Shira breathes shakily]
-[Fatima, in English] No!

120
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:28,100
[Fatima screams, echoes]

121
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,810
[Sitara gasps]

122
00:08:45,070 --> 00:08:46,160
[SITARA] Uh...

123
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:48,910
-Mistress?
-[Fatima breathes weakly]

124
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:54,910
Don't you...

125
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:57,920
dare touch...

126
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,750
[breathes shakily]

127
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:04,590
my beloved daughter.

128
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,180
[Sitara whimpers]

129
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:08,890
Mistress?

130
00:09:09,470 --> 00:09:13,520
Mistress? Mistress! [cries]

131
00:09:14,890 --> 00:09:16,810
[wails]

132
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,280
♪

133
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:37,540
[Sitara gasps softly]

134
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,260
[Sitara breathes shakily]

135
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,900
[SITARA] Uh?

136
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,640
[SITARA] Uh?

137
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,110
[ANIS] Uh?

138
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,650
Sitara?

139
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:49,030
[Zumurrud gasps]

140
00:10:49,070 --> 00:10:50,240
[Anis gasps]

141
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,450
[ANIS] Oh, you're alive.

142
00:10:56,410 --> 00:10:57,870
Are you hurt?

143
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,630
Ms. Anis, I... I, uh...

144
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:06,630
[tearfully]
I didn't keep my promise...

145
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:09,510
to keep the Mistress safe.

146
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:11,340
-The Mistress is...
-[Sitara cries]

147
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:13,600
[ANIS] Oh...

148
00:11:16,810 --> 00:11:18,810
They had captured us

149
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:21,520
as we were all making our way
up to the mountains.

150
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,270
[Zumurrud and Anis laugh]

151
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:25,980
[both gasp]

152
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:29,690
[ANIS] After that, we were
divided into smaller groups.

153
00:11:30,570 --> 00:11:34,370
Women, children,
and skilled craftsmen.

154
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:38,410
Then, the men and the elderly
were rounded up

155
00:11:38,450 --> 00:11:40,330
and taken away somewhere.

156
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:43,040
We haven't seen Uncle since.

157
00:11:45,630 --> 00:11:46,710
And then...

158
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:48,750
[men groaning]

159
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:52,470
[Zumurrud cries] Mikhail!

160
00:12:02,350 --> 00:12:04,560
[cries] Mikhail!

161
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:07,230
[SITARA] Oh, no.

162
00:12:08,690 --> 00:12:10,400
Ms. Zumurrud...

163
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,660
[cries]

164
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,410
[in English] Please, you have to
stop crying. [shushes]

165
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,040
Now be a good baby.

166
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,420
Ms. Zumurrud...

167
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,250
can you stand?

168
00:12:26,290 --> 00:12:28,670
-[horse neighs]
-[grunting]

169
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:30,380
[ANIS] Have you got her?

170
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,180
[SITARA] Uh?

171
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:41,100
I know him.

172
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:45,100
He's the ironmonger who fixed
that water basin for us.

173
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:49,400
We must find Uncle
and the others soon!

174
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,610
[woman screaming]

175
00:12:56,910 --> 00:13:00,030
[gasps] Hasan! Hasan!

176
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:04,460
[woman groans]

177
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:06,920
[SOLDIER] Chuu!

178
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:12,970
[SITARA (ADULT)] Their fear
of these mysterious men

179
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:18,550
spurred Sitara and the others
forward into the vast wasteland.

180
00:13:22,390 --> 00:13:24,640
[SITARA] This year,
the month of Safar

181
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,440
still feels a little chilly,

182
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,150
so the water is cold.

183
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,690
Although...

184
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:33,110
when the sun is out,

185
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:36,530
I see the rose buds
are already starting to swell.

186
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:42,750
As Anis and I are doing
our chores...

187
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:45,210
[CHILDREN]
"In the mighty name of Allah,

188
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:46,910
the Most Gracious..."

189
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,630
[SITARA] We can hear
Uncle's students

190
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,750
practicing their
recitation together.

191
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:53,050
-How adorable.
-[Sitara chuckles]

192
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:56,260
It reminds me
of when I first came out here!

193
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:58,340
[exclaims]

194
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,010
They've returned!

195
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:04,060
Hello, Mistress, welcome home!

196
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,430
So how was the bazaar today?

197
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,980
Thanks to Zumurrud,

198
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:10,020
I found quite a few
bargains there.

199
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:12,650
That's because I'm always
at your service.

200
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:15,240
[Fatima laughs] That's true.

201
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:17,820
Sitara, you'll have to
come with us next time.

202
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:18,950
Great!

203
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:22,080
By the way, I just sent a letter
off to Nishapur.

204
00:14:22,490 --> 00:14:25,750
As the roses bloom,
a reply might arrive.

205
00:14:25,790 --> 00:14:27,120
[Sitara exclaims]

206
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:32,000
[SITARA] After Safar comes
the month of Rabi' al-Awwal,

207
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,710
when the roses bloom.

208
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,300
At least, when they should have.

209
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:38,680
[Sitara cries]

210
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:50,140
[ANIS] Zumurrud, you must eat
to keep up your energy.

211
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:51,230
[Zumurrud groans]

212
00:14:52,190 --> 00:14:54,440
And you as well.
So, go on then.

213
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:57,240
[SITARA] You have it, Ms. Anis.

214
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:58,400
[Anis exhales]

215
00:14:58,450 --> 00:14:59,860
[ANIS] Thank you.

216
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:02,910
But this share here
is all yours.

217
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,990
Hey, tell me.

218
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,620
Do you remember when I said

219
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:11,540
slaves don't get
to decide things for themselves?

220
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:14,340
[SITARA] Yes.

221
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:16,420
Viewed in another way,

222
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:20,220
it means slaves aren't
responsible for things, either.

223
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:24,390
For instance, even if one
were to commit a crime,

224
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:27,770
their punishment is only half
that of somebody who's free.

225
00:15:27,810 --> 00:15:29,020
[Sitara gasps softly]

226
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,230
[ANIS] I suppose
you could say they think

227
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:34,310
we aren't capable of answering
for our own behavior.

228
00:15:35,730 --> 00:15:39,360
When it comes to the Mistress,
you mustn't decide for yourself

229
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,490
whether you're
accountable or not.

230
00:15:43,070 --> 00:15:45,740
[Sitara cries]
Then who decides it?

231
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:48,830
There's no one left who can!

232
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:53,170
The Mistress or Uncle.
They're both... [cries]

233
00:15:53,210 --> 00:15:54,460
That's true.

234
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,130
Wait,

235
00:15:56,880 --> 00:16:00,840
there is still one person
who's in Nishapur.

236
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:04,680
[Sitara breathes shakily]

237
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,100
Yes, that's right.

238
00:16:08,970 --> 00:16:10,270
[Anis chuckles]

239
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:15,270
Master Muhammad's out there.
He's still alive!

240
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,400
[ANIS] That's right.

241
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:20,990
So, you see then.
We still have one person left.

242
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:22,740
[Sitara breathes shakily]

243
00:16:24,570 --> 00:16:25,740
[Anis chuckles softly]

244
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:34,250
We... [cries]

245
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:37,630
We do! [cries]

246
00:16:37,670 --> 00:16:39,710
[Zumurrud cries]

247
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:42,420
[SITARA (ADULT)] Soon...

248
00:16:42,470 --> 00:16:45,180
the prisoners continued
moving eastward.

249
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:48,100
Day after day,
they traveled...

250
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:55,100
...threading between mountains,
crossing rivers.

251
00:16:55,310 --> 00:16:58,980
And then, just as Safar
was ending...

252
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:08,200
[Sitara (adult), in English]
The caravan came to a stop,

253
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,200
arriving at a group of tents.

254
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:13,290
Pitched in a place
called Taloqan.

255
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:17,580
[sheep bleating]

256
00:17:18,590 --> 00:17:19,920
[GIRL] Uh?

257
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:25,380
[SITARA] There are people here
who aren't soldiers.

258
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,090
Could this be their city?

259
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:31,350
[CRAFTSMAN] Excuse me,
where do you all hail from?

260
00:17:31,390 --> 00:17:32,640
[all gasp]

261
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:33,890
From Tus.

262
00:17:33,930 --> 00:17:35,310
[craftsman breathes uneasily]

263
00:17:35,350 --> 00:17:37,350
[CRAFTSMAN] You mean
they even conquered Tus?

264
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,900
[breathes uneasily]
Where are you from?

265
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:41,270
They spared us.

266
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:44,240
After we identified ourselves
as skilled craftsmen,

267
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,950
they brought us down here...

268
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,410
[exhales]

269
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:48,950
...from Nishapur.

270
00:17:49,530 --> 00:17:50,660
[Sitara gasps]

271
00:17:50,910 --> 00:17:52,290
♪

272
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:54,830
[CRAFTSMAN] After we learned
the nomads were approaching,

273
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:57,000
we fortified our defenses.

274
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:03,340
Then at the very moment
they descended upon us,

275
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:06,800
a single arrow fired
from the ramparts.

276
00:18:07,090 --> 00:18:10,090
Found its mark and struck down
their commander.

277
00:18:13,770 --> 00:18:16,770
And in retaliation
for that one arrow,

278
00:18:16,810 --> 00:18:20,980
the city of Nishapur was
completely burned to the ground!

279
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:34,740
[Craftsman, in English]
We skilled craftsmen

280
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:36,870
are the only people
who survived.

281
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:39,540
The others,
even our children were...

282
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,090
[Sitara gasps softly]

283
00:18:42,750 --> 00:18:46,260
[SITARA] Master Muhammad
was in Nishapur.

284
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:53,350
Can't be...

285
00:18:53,390 --> 00:18:54,560
[Zumurrud grunts]

286
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,770
[all gasp]

287
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:58,310
[ANIS] Zumurrud!

288
00:18:58,350 --> 00:18:59,980
[SITARA] Ms. Zumurrud!

289
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:02,400
[Zumurrud groans]

290
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:04,690
Mikhail...

291
00:19:04,730 --> 00:19:05,980
Mikhail.

292
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:07,320
Uh?

293
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,280
Zumurrud.

294
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,870
[ZUMURRUD] The setting sun.

295
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:16,490
It's so bright,
isn't it, Mikhail?

296
00:19:16,910 --> 00:19:19,500
-[waves lapping]
-[birds screeching]

297
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:23,340
[ZUMURRUD] And so beautiful.

298
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,760
-[Sitara and Anis gasp]
-[SITARA] Ms. Zumurrud!

299
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:29,050
[ANIS] Please, no!

300
00:19:29,090 --> 00:19:30,510
Don't leave us!

301
00:19:30,550 --> 00:19:32,180
I'm begging of you!

302
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:33,930
[both crying]

303
00:19:33,970 --> 00:19:36,680
[SITARA] Ms. Zumurrud
came from a distant land

304
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,980
where she could watch the sea!

305
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:43,190
She served the mistress
longer than any of us.

306
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:47,940
Did she want to return
there the whole time?

307
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:52,200
Did she miss her family
the whole time?

308
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,070
[Sitara cries]

309
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:59,910
[ANIS] We must give her
a proper burial at least.

310
00:20:00,370 --> 00:20:03,830
And reunite her
with her brother.

311
00:20:04,790 --> 00:20:07,750
[SITARA] "Indeed.
We all belong to Allah."

312
00:20:08,050 --> 00:20:11,920
[ALL] "And indeed,
to Him we shall return."

313
00:20:23,730 --> 00:20:25,230
[Sitara snores]

314
00:20:27,150 --> 00:20:30,110
Now there is no joy.

315
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:38,660
-[birds chirping]
-[flock bleating]

316
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,620
[WOMAN 1] Poor thing.

317
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:42,120
[WOMAN 2] What happened?

318
00:20:42,370 --> 00:20:43,540
[Sitara gasps]

319
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:45,040
Excuse me.

320
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,040
[gasps]

321
00:20:47,210 --> 00:20:49,710
[WOMAN 1] She lunged
at a soldier who was walking by.

322
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:50,760
[Sitara gasps]

323
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:52,590
And then he just
struck her down.

324
00:20:52,630 --> 00:20:54,180
[WOMAN 2] How dreadful!

325
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:56,510
So why is everyone just...

326
00:20:59,010 --> 00:21:00,970
[CRAFTSMAN]
Peace be upon her soul.

327
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:05,560
[SITARA]
She decided for herself.

328
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:08,110
Rather than becoming a slave
to the nomads

329
00:21:08,150 --> 00:21:09,820
for the rest of her life,

330
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:11,530
Ms. Anis wanted to die

331
00:21:11,570 --> 00:21:15,530
while she was still a slave
to her Tus family.

332
00:21:19,990 --> 00:21:21,370
I know.

333
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:24,330
If I keep walking
straight ahead,

334
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,500
maybe someone will shoot
an arrow into me.

335
00:21:33,130 --> 00:21:34,260
[SHIRA] Wait!

336
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,550
[Sitara gasps]

337
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:38,220
[SITARA] It's that boy.

338
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,850
[Sitara grunting]

339
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:45,810
[Shira grunts]

340
00:21:46,690 --> 00:21:48,520
It's not... it's not like that!

341
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:50,440
-Hey, listen!
-[Sitara crying]

342
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,980
You wanna get that book back,
don't you?

343
00:21:57,450 --> 00:21:59,160
[Sitara gasps softly]

344
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,620
[♪ closing theme song playing]

345
00:23:32,420 --> 00:23:35,380
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"An Undying Flame."

